# ACIQ — generated data, run artefacts, logs
data/*
# ...except the frozen v0 baseline, which must be versioned: it is the only
# measured evidence the project has, and the driver deletes each run directory
# before re-running.
!data/baselines/
data/baselines/*/
!data/baselines/v0/
!data/baselines/v0/**
testbed/logs/
*.log
# ...but the evidence is allowed to keep its logs.
#
# Order matters and this was silently wrong: `*.log` came *after* the
# `!data/baselines/v0/**` negation, and a later pattern wins. So every v0 log was
# excluded while SHA256SUMS still listed it -- the v0 README tells a reader to
# run `sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS`, and on a fresh clone that failed on 36 of 77
# files. The published repository's own documented verification step did not
# work.
!data/baselines/v0/**/*.log
!data/baselines/v0/**/*.sink.log

# The measured matrix and the first enforced runs are the project's evidence,
# the same argument as v0. Kept out of the working tree's transient output, not
# out of version control.
!data/matrix6/
!data/matrix6/**
!data/matrix6/**/*.log
!data/enforced/
!data/enforced/**
!data/enforced/**/*.log
!data/leased3/
!data/leased3/**
!data/leased3/**/*.log
!data/leaseA/
!data/leaseA/**
!data/leaseA/**/*.log
!data/leaseB/
!data/leaseB/**
!data/leaseB/**/*.log
!data/fixcheck/
!data/fixcheck/**
!data/fixcheck/**/*.log

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# Never commit real secrets. Only .env.example belongs in version control.
.env
*.key
*.pem

# docs/evidence is cited BY TRACKED DOCUMENTATION as the source of published
# numbers -- docs/PROJECT.md, docs/gap-closure/claim-audit.md and
# final-validation-report.md all name specific files in it. The blanket `*.log`
# rule above excluded them, so none of them was ever committed and a fresh clone
# got broken citations. Same failure the v0 comment above describes, one
# directory over. A later pattern wins, so the negation has to come after.
!docs/evidence/
!docs/evidence/**
!docs/evidence/**/*.log
!docs/evidence/**/*.json

# The lease A/B evidence is cited by name in the gap-closure reports (the
# Wilcoxon p-value and its seven paired seeds come from data/ab_lease_42), and
# `data/*` excluded it. Same defect as docs/evidence: the number is published,
# the data behind it is not.
!data/ab_lease/
!data/ab_lease/**
!data/ab_lease_42/
!data/ab_lease_42/**

# The host-gate evidence is the same case, and the same defect, one level up.
#
# docs/PROJECT_REPORT.md, docs/ACIQ_COMPLETE.md and
# docs/gap-closure/documentation-consistency.md publish the congested headline
# table (p50/p95/p99/jitter/loss for FIFO, CAKE95 and ACIQ) and the per-seed
# table, and name the directory the numbers come from:
#
#     data/host_gate_congested_aciq
#     data/host_gate_congested_b0_fifo
#     data/host_gate_congested_b1_cake95
#
# tools/reconcile_results.py re-derives every one of those numbers from the raw
# per-seed call.json files under exactly those directories, and
# tools/tail_analysis.py splits the per-packet trace in
# data/host_gate_congested_aciq into the transition and steady windows the
# report's tail section quotes. `data/*` excluded all of it, so the published
# numbers had no data behind them -- the identical failure the two comments
# above describe, for a third time, in a third directory.
#
# The claim "the committed data/host_gate_* runs carry revisions ..." was
# therefore false in the same way: nothing under data/host_gate_* had ever been
# committed. What is committed now is the current-revision run, and each
# directory carries a REVISION file naming the revision that produced it.
#
# A later pattern wins, so these negations must come after the blanket `data/*`
# and the blanket `*.log` rules above -- otherwise the logs are excluded again
# and the per-seed evidence is incomplete.
!data/host_gate_*/
!data/host_gate_*/**
!data/host_gate_*/**/*.log
!data/host_gate_*/**/*.json
!data/host_gate_*/**/*.jsonl

# The remaining run directories, and the acceptance logs, are the same case a
# fourth time.
#
# Every artifacts/validation/<rev>/acceptance.json that is published names the
# log each phase wrote -- unittest.log, gate.log, metric-integrity.log,
# claim-audit.log and the rest -- in its "log" field. All 289 of those
# references were broken: the JSON was published and the log it points at was
# not, so a reader who followed the pointer got a missing file. The gate result
# is only checkable if the log it claims to summarise is there.
#
# The same applies to testbed/logs/: docs/limitations.md names
# testbed/logs/gate-20261009-204709.log as the record of a specific traffic
# gate, and the other gate logs in that directory are the runs behind the
# published gate numbers.
#
# And the data/ run directories -- the lease A/B seed sets, the dev*/dropcheck*
# experiment series, the live and runs directories -- are the raw data behind
# the measurements the gap-closure reports discuss. They are small (a few
# hundred KB each) and they are the only place those numbers can be checked.
#
# A later pattern wins, so these negations come after the blanket `data/*` and
# `*.log` rules above. Without that ordering the logs are excluded again and
# the citations break once more.
!artifacts/validation/
!artifacts/validation/**
!artifacts/validation/**/*.log
!testbed/logs/
!testbed/logs/**
!testbed/logs/**/*.log
!data/ab_lease_*/
!data/ab_lease_*/**
!data/ab_lease_*/**/*.log
!data/ab_nolease*/
!data/ab_nolease_*/
!data/ab_nolease/**
!data/ab_nolease_/**
!data/ab_nolease/**/*.log
!data/ab_nolease_*/**/*.log
!data/dev*/
!data/dev*/**
!data/dev*/**/*.log
!data/dropcheck*/
!data/dropcheck*/**
!data/dropcheck*/**/*.log
!data/lease*/
!data/lease*/**
!data/lease*/**/*.log
!data/leased*/
!data/leased*/**
!data/leased*/**/*.log
!data/live/
!data/live/**
!data/live/**/*.log
!data/runs/
!data/runs/**
!data/runs/**/*.log
!data/REPORT.md
!data/COMPARISON.md
!data/host_gate_*/**
